# Flip-Flop Lab Enhancement & Verification Plan

An interactive digital electronics learning platform featuring 3D Three.js PCB simulation, 2D fallbacks, live truth tables, timing waveforms, step-by-step tutorials, and mastery quizzes for SR, JK, D, and T flip-flops.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The original project file was uploaded as `flipflop` without an `.html` file extension. We have created `index.html` to allow browsers and web servers to serve it properly. Both files can be maintained or `index.html` can be kept as the main entry point.

---

## 1. File Correctness & Audit Findings

We inspected the uploaded project and found the following issues:

1. **File Extension Missing**: The project was uploaded as a single file named `flipflop` without an `.html` extension. Web browsers, web servers (GitHub Pages, Netlify, Vercel), and local static file servers require `index.html` to serve and open it properly.
2. **Duplicate JavaScript Function**: `showLogic()` was defined twice (lines 1462 and 1476). The first definition was an outdated version missing edge direction indicators (`rising ↑` / `falling ↓`).
3. **Dead DOM Queries**: `setAuto()` looked for `#clk-auto` and `#home-clock`, but the dock controls dynamically render buttons with `[data-act="auto"]`.
4. **WebGL Texture Dimension Warning**: In `textSprite()`, canvas dimensions `256x72` are non-power-of-two, causing WebGL warnings (`THREE.WebGLRenderer: Texture has been resized from (256x72) to (256x64)`).
5. **Missing Favicon**: Browser requested `/favicon.ico` resulting in 404 errors. An inline SVG data URI favicon will resolve this cleanly.
6. **Fixed Clock Rate**: Auto clock period is hardcoded to 800ms without user control over clock speed.

